{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "איפה הם רעים", :translit "eifah heim ro'im", :gloss "where are they feeding / do they feed the flock"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling (missing vav in רעים) links phonetically to רעה = evil"}], :frame {:text "Jeroboam son of Nebat was made king over Israel in Shechem (1 Kings 12:1, 12:20). He inaugurated calf-worship at Bethel and Dan, causing Israel to sin (1 Kings 12:28-30), and is condemned throughout Kings as the archetype of evil leadership (1 Kings 13:34). Shechem, the very city of this verse (Genesis 37:12-14), thus becomes the site where royal evil originated.", :sources ["1 Kings 12:1" "1 Kings 12:20" "1 Kings 12:28-30" "1 Kings 13:34" "Genesis 37:12-14"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling (missing vav in רעים) links phonetically to רעה = evil", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:10:23.017120963Z", :model "glm-5.2"}